  "contract": [
    "Null allocation delegates to the native public allocator. Nonnull allocation with null pool or failing range check returns null without invoking allocator failure policy.",
    "Existing allocations use native unsigned rounding without the public malloc minimum clamp. A16-byte-or-larger remainder is split with retained low flag bits, and the tail is released through native free.",
    "Growth allocates, reloads the original header, copies the full old block payload capacity byte by byte in increasing order, then frees the original. It inherits the public non-returning exhaustion policy.",
    "This private firmware resize entry is not an alias for libc realloc or the portable heap model."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "All152 native instruction bytes execute in20,928 comparisons, including3,072 terminal growth failures.36 additional pointer/null-pool cases are checked. Seeded nonzero full payload capacities expose padding-copy behavior.",
    "1000 mixed operations execute only C initializer/malloc/free/resize on the source side, including295 resizes. No stock allocation fallback. Pool images and write width/order/value match. The mixed sequence uses resize sizes at least8; zero-size metadata behavior is tested in isolated comparisons.",
    "Returning paths check saved integer/FP registers, SP, masks/FPSCR and guards. Terminal paths check guards, FP/masks and stable delay-loop depth while status/log/watchdog/RTOS/delay ports are modeled and stopped after three delays.",
    "Ten compiled defects are rejected. Caller scratch, private frames, APSR, malformed headers, arbitrary interior pointers, near-wrap huge physical copies, concurrent mutation, real manager reset, physical memory behavior, final linking/startup and boot remain unverified.",
    "One new C unit with no state or import changes. Existing native heap providers and portable model objects are unchanged. Source plan/cache layout unchanged. Deinitialization and complete source-linked firmware remain open."
